Jumping is the cheapest spellbook to write. Write it and then enhance
escape spells to basic; at basic, spell jumping is even better than
jumping boots. You can even jump while burdened! The only drawback is
that a regular lamp doesn't give quite enough light for basic jumping.
You may need the Candelabrum or spell of light as a light source on
Astral and the Sanctum.

As for the sanctum itself, if you have plenty of scrolls, levelport
inside after the invocation to get closer to the Amulet. I believe a
ring of conflict can slow the crowds down when you're using the
jumping/teleport strategy, since they'll stay in their positions
fighting each other instead of surrounding you.

And most of all, if you're using jumping, make sure you have royal
jelly or K-rations or some such goodies in your bag. You'll need food.

